# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

TanStack Start + Cloudflare Workers + D1 + Drizzle + Better Auth.

## Develop

```sh
npm install
npm run dev                  # vite dev on :3000 (loads .dev.vars)
```

`npm run dev` boots Vite with the Cloudflare plugin; miniflare provides the
local D1 binding (`DB`). HMR + SSR both work.

## Database

```sh
npm run db:generate          # drizzle-kit: schema -> SQL migration in drizzle/
npm run db:migrate:local     # apply migrations to miniflare's local D1
npm run test:contract        # cascade-FK contract test
```

Schema lives at `src/db/schema.ts`. Every user-owned table MUST declare
`references(() => user.id, { onDelete: 'cascade' })` on its FK; the contract
test enforces this. The cascade fires when Better Auth's `/api/auth/delete-user`
endpoint runs.

## Build / preview

```sh
npm run build                # vite build -> dist/
npm run preview              # npm run build && vite preview
```

The production build is what `wrangler deploy` ships. Preview is the closest
local mirror of prod runtime behavior — security headers are applied there
(they're skipped under `vite dev`, see `src/lib/security-headers.ts`).

## Secrets / env vars

Local dev reads `.dev.vars` (gitignored). See `.env.example` for the full
list — at minimum:

- `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` — 32-byte hex; auto-generated by the install step.
- `BETTER_AUTH_URL` — public URL of the auth handler. `http://localhost:3000`
  in dev.
- `LOG_LEVEL` — `debug` / `info` / `warn` / `error`. Default `info`.

For production, run `wrangler secret put <NAME>` for each. Public (non-secret)
vars can live in `wrangler.jsonc` under `vars`.

## Observability

Every request gets a 12-char `X-Request-Id`. The server entry (`src/server.ts`)
wraps the handler in AsyncLocalStorage so `log.info(...)` etc. (from
`src/lib/log.ts`) emit structured JSON lines with that ID — captured by
Cloudflare Workers' built-in observability in prod, and printed to stdout in
dev. When debugging a user-reported error, ask them for the request ID and
grep logs for it.

## Routing layout

File-based routing via TanStack Router. Conventions in use:

- `src/routes/__root.tsx` — root layout + global error boundary + 404 page.
- `src/routes/_marketing/` — pathless layout for public pages
  (`/`, `/pricing`, `/resources`, `/terms`, `/privacy`).
- `src/routes/(auth)/` — route group for `/sign-in` and `/sign-up`.
- `src/routes/dashboard/` — auth-gated app surface.
- `src/routes/api/auth/$.ts` — Better Auth catch-all.

## Deploy

Deploys are owned by the supertools-design `deploy` concern, not by this
template. The template ships a working local app; the deploy concern provisions
D1, sets secrets via `wrangler secret put`, and runs `wrangler deploy`.
